# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/target

# What packaging produces (AppImage, zip): binaries are not committed
/dist
*.AppImage

# Backups / debug
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode (the gate scripts live in tools/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
*~

# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed - this is a workspace with a binary, and a reproducible build matters more.
# Not ignored.

# Generated G-code (the examples)
examples/*.tap
*.tap

# SCRATCH MEASUREMENTS AGAINST PERSONAL DOCUMENTS - they do not belong in the repository.
# They reach into files outside the tree by absolute paths and build nowhere except on one machine. Such a
# file once went into a commit through `git add -A`, so what holds the rule now is this line rather than
# memory. The crate that held them is gone; the pattern stays, because the habit is what it guards against.
**/zzz_*.rs
**/the_users_*.rs

# Crash reports and gathered problem reports, if anyone ever points the program at the tree.
crashes/
reports/

# The list of crate sources for Flatpak: generated from Cargo.lock by packaging/flatpak/update-manifest.sh
# before a submission. Not kept here - it goes stale at every change of the lock file, and a stale list of
# sources is worse than none: the build stops halfway with a message about being offline.
packaging/flatpak/cargo-sources.json

# autosaves the program writes beside an open project (a probe opening a sample writes them too)
*.autosave.qcad
*.autosave.qcad.bak

# Personal notes for the coding assistant, kept on the owner's machine
CLAUDE.local.md

# Samples that cannot be distributed: a link to them in a working copy, checks pass them over when absent
/samples
